# <%= className %> scheduler

Location: `apps/<%= fileName %>`. NestJS headless worker (`createApplicationContext`,
no HTTP) with `@nestjs/schedule`.

## Layout

- `src/app.module.ts` — imports `ScheduleModule.forRoot()`, registers `TasksService`.
- `src/tasks.service.ts` — the jobs. One decorated method per job.
- `src/main.ts` — boots the app context and enables shutdown hooks. Scheduled
  jobs keep the process alive.

## Adding a job

Add a method to a provider and decorate it:

- `@Cron('*/5 * * * *', { name: 'foo' })` or `@Cron(CronExpression.EVERY_HOUR)` — cron schedule.
- `@Interval('foo', 10_000)` — every N ms.
- `@Timeout('foo', 5_000)` — once, N ms after start.

Always pass a `name` so the job can be found/paused via `SchedulerRegistry`.
Keep handlers thin and idempotent — a missed or repeated run must be safe.
Use `@nestjs/config` for schedules that differ per environment.

## Running

```bash
nx serve <%= fileName %>      # nest start --watch
nx build <%= fileName %>
nx test <%= fileName %>
```

Deps are not installed by the generator — run `npm install` in `apps/<%= fileName %>` first.
